A||||16||JohnnyK||Won't shift to 1st while moving||||5||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||03-19-2000||11:49 PM||||For some reason, once I start slowing down, I cannot downshift into 1st gear... (The stick physically won't move into there)... It will downshift to all the other gears, but won't go to 1st? I basically have to be at a complete standstill, and then it will go (well, I DO have to be at a complete standstill  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> .... Any ideas? Thanks<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Gokart||03-20-2000||05:33 AM||||Why would you want to downshift into 1st while the car is moving anyway? Isn't that not a good idea?||||reg||5
Z||000002||JohnnyK||03-20-2000||01:30 PM||||Well, I can't exactly inch the car up my drive way in 3rd..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||03-20-2000||01:43 PM||||Bet you've got a 4-speed!  It's really tough to get a 4-speed Muncie into 1st gear unless you've come to a complete stop - that's just the nature of the beast.  Either 5-speed (Isuzu or Getrag) should ease into 1st with no problem if you're rolling along at 5 mph or so.<P>The Haynes Fiero manual has a really good procedure for adjusting the shift linkage, which could help you out.  I know a guy with an 85 GT who followed it and it made a world of difference to his 4-speed.  It really helped his 2-3 upshift and 3-2 downshift.||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||03-20-2000||05:22 PM||||I've found it's earier to go into first gear if you visit second gear first (don't have to let the clutch out).||||reg||1
Z||000005||Patrick||03-20-2000||07:02 PM||||<BR>Will it downshift if you <I>double-clutch</I>?<P>If you need to ask what double-clutching is, we'll have to take your Fiero away... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000006||SCCA FIERO||03-20-2000||07:08 PM||||With my old 4 speed I would have to give it some gas to bring the revs up for the synchros to match. Just blip the gas with the clutch in and holding the shifter against 1st gear... should go.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Carrolles||03-20-2000||07:24 PM||||My 85se v-6 with the muncie 4spd shifts great with 125000 miles on it.  I never have trouble downshifting to first gear.||||reg||1
Z||000008||JohnnyK||03-20-2000||09:54 PM||||Jesus.. It's a 5 speed..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||batboy||03-20-2000||10:14 PM||||Oh. Never mind.||||reg||1
Z||000010||ChadMan||03-21-2000||08:40 AM||||Johnny, I'd guess your linkage is fudged up then.  I'd try adjusting it using the Haynes method.<P>Filthy transaxle fluid can cause balky shifting, too.||||reg||1
Z||000011||DRH||03-21-2000||01:48 PM||||I would try changing the fluid and adjusting the linkage as mentioned above. If fluid and linkage are right, then that pretty much leaves the syncronizer. <P>Try matching engine speed to wheel speed as mentioned by SCCA Fiero above. If that does the trick it is either synco fix time (big $$$) or learn to do the speed match thing (free  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ).<P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||mwbackus||03-21-2000||02:40 PM||||Another case of failure with the thin-air mind reading subsystem.  If you dont specify the model, year, engine, or trans type that you are referring to, how can you expect to get an accurate evaluation of the problem?  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||theogre||03-21-2000||08:10 PM||||A syncro could be a problem, but then there might be no problem at all. not going into first while in motion is common to allot of trannys. Allot of it depends on just what set of gears is in the tranny.<P>My fords used to do this. 2 exactly identical trannys, good oil, good hardware, same motor, same rear gears, except first gear in one tranny was lower than the other. The one with the lower gear absolutly would not drop into first above 3-5mph. The other would easily drop into 1st as high as 10-12mph.<P>With a low first gear this is kind of a good thing if annoying at a few times. A low first gear can easily explode a clutch disk if it goes in at to high a speed.||||reg||1
